<<~ ahu slot=`#/rank-consensus`>>

!! Rank consensus ~ several lenses over one item set

''The fold.'' Several strict, best-first rankings over the SAME named items yield one reproducible order. Each ranking names every item exactly once; an absent or repeated item stops the fold rather than inviting a guessed position. The first ranking supplies the stable tie order.

''Two readings.'' Borda adds each item's zero-based positions and advances the lowest sum, a tied sum following the first ranking's order (`bordaConsensus`). Kemeny searches the permutations for the order with the least total Kendall-tau pair disagreement (`kemenyConsensus`, `kendallTauCost`); seeded with Borda and keeping the first equal-cost order, its disagreement never exceeds Borda's. Exhaustive search reaches at most eight items (`KEMENY_MAX_ITEMS`); a larger set takes another method or a refusal, never an unbounded silent search (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/rank-consensus.ts`).

''The ladder boundary.'' Aperture, the action ladder, scope, rating and stage each name a vocabulary of their own, so their five rows rank no shared set of candidates. A caller first names the common candidates and takes a strict order over them from each lens it means to fold. Without that mapping, the separate readings stand side by side and no consensus gets announced.

''The authority boundary.'' A consensus order compresses the disagreement among the readings it received; it grants no federation rank, gate authority or world verdict. The input orders and the Kendall cost ride beside the result, so another reader can inspect what the fold moved.

<<~/ahu>>

